#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "446ea007-1ff4-5023-8e3f-7f00eb0fb2d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5071" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/e5e3e1baad54a5ce65047fbcb5e7a58d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3$. Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{5^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{3^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{25} + \\frac{y^{2}}{9} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "af56117c-65e0-5f12-9780-7a95e6be829e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5072" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/10eddd924b3dc68fbf1bb4eaeb8f92c5.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4$. Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{2^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{16} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "b7c94673-f847-5977-9b9f-8d235ea42eb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5073" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} + \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1$?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nIn the given equation, we have $a^2=36$ and $b^2=25$.\n\n- Since $a^2=36$, the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36} = 6$.\n- Since $b^2=25$, the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5$.\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=6$, and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5$.\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length\n\n$$\n2a = 2 \\cdot 6 = 12\n$$\n\nand the minor axis has length\n\n$$\n2b = 2 \\cdot 5 =10\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ab69723-4124-51c1-8a26-99a155e4819f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267426} {:answer/id #uuid "4a34e8d7-aef1-5c9c-833d-fd39e67149e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267427} {:answer/id #uuid "b3511758-ceda-5811-b808-1a9017e77f22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267428} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5d08e9-a5a8-5b40-8683-2d9e7ed0fa29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267429} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf4ba50-2e6a-5c79-b044-946c8793b726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bf4ba50-2e6a-5c79-b044-946c8793b726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267430} :answer-field/id #uuid "04ea4c3f-0ebe-503f-a8ab-a5f196a4632c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "121eae13-33e3-557f-b14a-45dd0565e764" :question/math-academy-id "q-115124" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/764f25a4b18f3f28110c0ce3345402bf183d61cac350832663e221b0de9852a5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f215864-38d7-566c-afe9-4a09a161b6c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$16$ and $7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267433} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1dc458-056c-5463-a63e-9f9a5bd73b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267434} {:answer/id #uuid "988e8122-5f7d-53fd-b2d6-d09a8e724da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $2\\sqrt{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267435} {:answer/id #uuid "0131ef0e-e2eb-536a-be1d-c1cf86b47462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $3.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267436} {:answer/id #uuid "903ced79-a4fa-5ff0-a803-c8a0e389da64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $\\sqrt{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "988e8122-5f7d-53fd-b2d6-d09a8e724da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $2\\sqrt{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267435} :answer-field/id #uuid "31547c68-b82b-54d7-8f55-8afad5840962" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267432}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02c6473a-43c5-5274-9b53-50a0ccd1fa94" :question/math-academy-id "q-115132" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56dd600f-8737-5a97-af81-302fdbf3038c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$28$ and $24$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267440} {:answer/id #uuid "9fdb9382-5d19-542d-8947-5e8d5bde2cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$24.5$ and $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267441} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6c0040-a1a8-5b8e-bea9-b287003e0e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ and $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267442} {:answer/id #uuid "5edb0aa2-5781-5407-8c2c-8eb589de64b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$49$ and $36$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267443} {:answer/id #uuid "c0784555-d64b-530f-a8ee-d99b128e6f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea6c0040-a1a8-5b8e-bea9-b287003e0e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ and $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267442} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce852cca-c1f2-541f-815e-eb611ba8f808" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267439}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3113828e-6ca6-530b-804d-2cdc91aade73" :question/math-academy-id "q-115134" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cd513c-0f75-5c1f-b46c-45e80c3719c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267447} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7d5c88-1459-536c-b6da-74258ee639fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267448} {:answer/id #uuid "2da80e4f-bebd-5d21-bbbf-0441a5bd9e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267449} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd22e77-097f-5aed-a9f0-69d727c4148f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267450} {:answer/id #uuid "da0b1065-0ffd-54b2-a18a-78cfcc4ec9da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd22e77-097f-5aed-a9f0-69d727c4148f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267450} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb2af5e-054b-59f7-be64-d428bf579b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20f799f9-37ea-5b3e-b820-5abed8180539" :question/math-academy-id "q-16451" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/6116ecf00a26d9828b238879b61385c1296f33ff863dbb8337a3b22be5981f10.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe36d33d-c023-5687-80ec-3082a05294fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267454} {:answer/id #uuid "e6332e69-af63-5c7b-bc00-6ee0bb4d2b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267455} {:answer/id #uuid "967eea40-f5c2-5dc8-8973-b6d75547cb4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267456} {:answer/id #uuid "b7847be4-3c62-5d1f-bb59-472e843e9c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267457} {:answer/id #uuid "b3051afd-3369-59bd-857a-0e2ff2ba6166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "967eea40-f5c2-5dc8-8973-b6d75547cb4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267456} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9918978-8f69-5750-8d91-a9c1f31b369c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267453}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90e9eb4e-4291-5a98-8dd4-1b3680d6b660" :question/math-academy-id "q-16454" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=12.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=12,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5acf0a59-294d-5456-a08e-08843fd6431b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5acf0a59-294d-5456-a08e-08843fd6431b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267461} :answer-field/id #uuid "19779c6c-fe73-51b9-803e-83f35b86068d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02046be2-6e9e-58e2-9820-43fe5a67973a" :question/math-academy-id "q-277921" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/ab3d1fefcefa12133ec4ea7e3e6ce744c88f5a9b25029c950254706097cb4c4d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baa35645-ef47-5f54-9b9e-4c07e364a093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{64}+\\frac{y^2}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267464} {:answer/id #uuid "7416161e-e86b-5694-a527-5a696a385ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{y^2}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baa35645-ef47-5f54-9b9e-4c07e364a093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{64}+\\frac{y^2}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267464} :answer-field/id #uuid "cca126d1-3161-54e3-a5f5-e41fb4e883ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267463}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "012b63f2-36d4-5ed9-a297-1a5f74a1ead6" :question/math-academy-id "q-279101" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/eb9c9b61de232ab6c190a3a324ff3ee2515c61f72a16e2814d77f94a60255501.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=8$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "662089c0-2288-59c0-bb6b-d751952e370b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{30.25}+\\frac{y^2}{2.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "662089c0-2288-59c0-bb6b-d751952e370b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{30.25}+\\frac{y^2}{2.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267468} :answer-field/id #uuid "c174abfc-8652-5116-9ac6-2aa9d293cd98" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267467}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35f548a2-d6c8-5a3e-9a21-576d6ab82182" :question/math-academy-id "q-279126" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/410a33acd13bc05e65a8f11defb9828a68bf5b80826305adefe2d008afa245c4.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{11}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{121}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a647912-c16b-5e40-ad59-0408e3372757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{20.25}+\\frac{y^2}{42.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a647912-c16b-5e40-ad59-0408e3372757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{20.25}+\\frac{y^2}{42.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267471} :answer-field/id #uuid "c468d3ab-b1fd-53bc-80c5-b5eadbfb22d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267470}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fa0f7da-6dac-5383-8bb1-c2e631b620a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-279158" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/c583eabd1719e94dc727b876b944c839a39124adb341d88357cf954dbed79646.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{9}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{13}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{13}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{169}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{169} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7548eafc-7df5-5afb-a297-1e1005ac2880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7548eafc-7df5-5afb-a297-1e1005ac2880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267474} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d0b79c-4e9f-5ee7-b80c-118a07d50d3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dee65f6-b01a-5c75-ba21-bd7419c0b0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dee65f6-b01a-5c75-ba21-bd7419c0b0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267476} :answer-field/id #uuid "76332875-348e-59c2-9b72-ad29c378231b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267475}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f65fdb1-916c-5738-a316-a9718e63430b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279169" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d5c9d1-3c82-5af9-aae2-bff5ea543677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267479} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac19654-e9cf-5cbc-ad79-5e17c5cf6676" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267480} {:answer/id #uuid "0e30b6dc-9b27-56f4-bac6-239acae40580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267481} {:answer/id #uuid "384e03ef-b31d-57fa-a817-8e57e5fc9381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267482} {:answer/id #uuid "1e277316-bfd8-578b-903a-06f63e69e1a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22d5c9d1-3c82-5af9-aae2-bff5ea543677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267479} :answer-field/id #uuid "8980ee0c-1a37-52e1-82df-a8bf77fa947e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b66b9a52-af69-562e-9a8f-594e2cdd513a" :question/math-academy-id "q-69891" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/9eb144bd4109846f3e1af4fb7d8ed70d2d8a29c3804547b89238d6437c4258d8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e550c211-498b-5d23-ad61-88713a441473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267486} {:answer/id #uuid "522d2b6a-06a3-5c61-a3d8-6456ce8df6f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267487} {:answer/id #uuid "79f75e94-1313-50e0-a16f-b18eac472ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267488} {:answer/id #uuid "4c15bf74-8142-595e-817e-71cd41315d16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267489} {:answer/id #uuid "74e693b5-790f-5cac-aa12-6cde74ccd18d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c15bf74-8142-595e-817e-71cd41315d16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267489} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee700f7d-06d6-52b2-bb6c-cfd0351d4586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267485}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8326fb9-0def-51c9-820d-44bddbba92c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-69892" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/1acc2d6b8387947ff7186322796e273bcec366810ad73ac0025494ab627e06b2.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=1$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec17315-ecea-5a46-86b9-10826fc86f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267493} {:answer/id #uuid "709bd1aa-6289-5f10-a063-81c1ac15b7ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267494} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc5aca1-cf29-5761-be5f-7bdf0e50b9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267495} {:answer/id #uuid "3f96ca79-5e37-5709-a2c2-fb41f6a9e901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267496} {:answer/id #uuid "4c823ea5-1ab4-51c8-9be9-6254583d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bc5aca1-cf29-5761-be5f-7bdf0e50b9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab01a51-dea6-54fe-8d4a-a18973f2a125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267492}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75a4ea63-60ed-555d-b33c-9e409712e1e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73619" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/8637901efc126236b190e7012cf65a06be078cb21c3093eff39b927493000138.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1.5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{2}})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfe58789-fd77-57f3-bbce-f97e5dd67d1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267500} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8ae039-2e0c-5b27-928b-48dca10ec333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267501} {:answer/id #uuid "361238c6-97cd-571f-a264-f1595fc97bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267502} {:answer/id #uuid "fc5b7510-1302-5aca-a005-6b58e2a7e35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267503} {:answer/id #uuid "dafdf6e3-8816-5d7a-9aae-28d3972e49d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dafdf6e3-8816-5d7a-9aae-28d3972e49d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267504} :answer-field/id #uuid "322998a7-489e-5edf-b86e-8a485dead1e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267499}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "480a616c-8c80-5f81-b3d5-aa7488c0665b" :question/math-academy-id "q-7596" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=18.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=18,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=3\\sqrt{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}=6\\sqrt{2},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81292d50-5c51-5b38-89f0-949bc6b6a964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086540} {:answer/id #uuid "0c18f3df-95fb-536c-8e2f-3029a38b2427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086541} {:answer/id #uuid "1e67014b-0d00-54c0-af93-fd3ae84e9b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086542} {:answer/id #uuid "3c28a557-2851-503b-97be-c5d293379692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{16} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086543} {:answer/id #uuid "7affd3de-ff29-5c52-853b-6c179253ff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7affd3de-ff29-5c52-853b-6c179253ff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086544} :answer-field/id #uuid "92982adf-0bda-5979-982f-53887542631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086539}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "808bb938-3f2e-5c94-82a4-205181f5d6ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-7604" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/q-7604.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
